 173| 
 174| ## 5. Mode definitions
 175| 
 176| ### 5.1 Non-interactive (prompt → result)
 177| 
 178| **Intent:** Live interaction is unnecessary. One brief, one child run, structured artifacts. **Cheapest correct path.**
 179| 
 180| **Parent does**
 181| 
 182| 1. Write brief (existing template: Task, Acceptance, Constraints, Evidence).
 183| 2. Mode is auto or pinned NI.
 184| 3. `exec` native one-shot (D7), including allowed reliability wrappers (preflight / quota-retry / tail-idle). Block on exit (optional read-only `monitor.sh` on the log file — no second PTY). NI ignores `--max-wall-sec` (wall is wave-scoped for interactive; NI is block-on-exit). `--idle-sec` on NI feeds the D7 tail-idle watcher (same numeric value as interactive idle) (I-51).
 185| 4. Score PASS from exit code + log floor + evidence + commit policy.
 186| 5. Must not send follow-up keystrokes in this process.
 187| 6. If auto and miss → §4.2. If pin and miss → FAIL.
 188| 
 189| **Child transport (host native one-shot, no PTY)**
 190| 
 191| - Claude: `claude --print` (existing `--use-print` path).
 192| - Codex: `codex exec` (existing `--use-exec` path).
 193| - Cursor: `cursor-agent` print/stream-json (current default).
 194| - OpenCode: `opencode run` (current default).
 195| - Pi: `pi -p --provider opencode-go --model mimo-v2.5` (current default).
 196| 
 197| **Outputs (all hosts)**
 198| 
 199| - `.planning/agent-<host>/<task-id>/brief.md`
 200| - `run.log` (raw)
 201| - `result.md` (STATUS block per [`skills/silver-agent-worker/SKILL.md`](skills/silver-agent-worker/SKILL.md): `pass|fail|blocked` only — parent-scored incomplete is written as `fail` + `reason[]` `incomplete`; missing file is synthesized `fail` + `result-missing` (I-44). Fields: TASK, FILES, TESTS, COMMIT, BLOCKERS, NEXT_RETRY_PROMPT)
 202| - `mode.json` (`{requested, classified, resolved, reason[]}` — the only `mode_resolved` record in NI; **no** `events.jsonl`, **no** fifo; same core schema as the interactive `mode_resolved` event). When the I-56 fallback hop occurred, `reason[]` MUST contain `mode_fallback:interactive→non-interactive:<cause>:<via>`.
 203| - git delta / SHA when the brief requires code
 204| - `session.json` only if the host one-shot returns a reusable conversation id — omit the file when there is none (not an empty file). If written from NI, `status=dead` (resume-token only; not an in-wave `live` session); omit `turns` / `wave_started_at` (partial record is schema-valid; I-52/I-58)
 205| 
 206| ### 5.2 Interactive (parent drives TUI like a user)
 207| 
 208| **Intent:** A live session will improve the outcome, or the user pinned interactive, or auto NI already missed.
 209| 
 210| **Mental model:** Parent is a user at the child’s terminal: read the screen, type, wait, type again, until the task is done or escalated.
 211| 
 212| ```mermaid
 213| sequenceDiagram
 214|   participant Parent
 215|   participant Driver
 216|   participant ChildTUI
 217|   Parent->>Driver: start(interaction_mode=interactive, brief)
 218|   Driver->>ChildTUI: spawn PTY
 219|   loop until done or abort
 220|     ChildTUI-->>Driver: screen plus events
 221|     Driver-->>Parent: snapshot plus classified event
 222|     Parent->>Driver: send text or key
 223|     Driver->>ChildTUI: type as user
 224|   end
 225|   ChildTUI-->>Driver: exit
 226|   Driver-->>Parent: result.md plus logs
 227| ```
 228| 
 229| **Parent interaction loop (normative)**
 230| 
 231| 1. `start` — one PTY/session to the native TUI. Reuse `session.json` when D3 applies. Brief is typed like a user (not a second `--print` bolted onto a TUI).
 232| 2. On `ready` — submit brief (paste + Enter), matching existing E2E-081 submit-order (wake banner, then route, do not starve `/silver:*` / `$silver:*`).
 233| 3. On `assistant` / `tool_use` / `idle_working` — wait; optional heartbeat.
 234| 4. On `question` / `clarify` / `picker` — parent chooses from brief + policy; send keys (`Enter`, arrows, `y`/`n`, text).
 235| 5. On `stuck` / `zero_tokens` — parent may Enter-wake, re-paste a narrower instruction, or abort. One automatic wake is allowed; then parent decides (I-26).
 236| 6. On `auth` / `quota` — same escalation ladder as today; parent does not paste secrets.
 237| 7. On `done` — harvest STATUS / `result.md`; parent still verifies acceptance (child must not tell the user “done”).
 238| 8. Parent may inject **coaching turns** (“tests failed, fix X”) until timeout or `--max-turns`.
 239|    - **`tui` hosts (Claude / Codex / OpenCode / Pi-if-TUI):** coaching stays in the **same process / PTY** — no new-process coaching.
 240|    - **Cursor `session` transport (I-6):** a follow-up **is a new process** that reuses the host session / conversation id. That is the Cursor interactive equivalent, not a D5/D7 violation, and not `mode-unavailable`.
 241| 
 242| **Hard limits**
 243| 
 244| - `--max-turns` default 8 (brief submit counts as 1). Persist `{turns, wave_started_at}` on interactive `session.json` / `mode.json` (omit both on NI resume-token `session.json`; I-58) so Cursor new-process follow-ups share one wave counter (I-24).
 245| - `--max-wall-sec` host defaults (Claude/Codex 900, Cursor 1800, OpenCode/Pi 900), **wave-scoped** not per-process.
 246| - `--idle-sec` before `stuck` event (reuse existing quiet/idle env).
 247| - No credential paste. Brief secret scan unchanged.
 248| 
 249| ## 6. Shared API
 250| 
 251| ### 6.1 Skill / slash
 252| 
 253| ```
 254| /silver:agent-<host> <brief> [--interaction-mode auto|interactive|non-interactive]
 255|   [--mode permissive|strict]
 256|   [--work-dir <path>] [--log <path>] [--attach]
 257|   [--max-turns N] [--max-wall-sec N] [--idle-sec N] [--allow-mode-fallback] [--no-escalate]
 258| ```
 259| 
 260| Update `argument-hint` on all five SKILL.md files. `--mode` = permission only.
 261| 
 262| **When auto picks which**
 263| 
 264| - Interactive: session would improve output (D3), or likely Q&A/pickers/coaching.
 265| - Non-interactive: bounded implement-and-report (including first-wave implement+test), no need to keep the child brain.
 266| - User pin always wins (including over D3).
 267| 
 268| ### 6.2 CLI (every `invoke.sh` + `*-delegate.sh`)
 269| 
 270| ```
 271| --interaction-mode auto|interactive|non-interactive   # default auto; NOT --mode
 272| --mode permissive|strict                              # permission only (existing); orthogonal
 273| --interactive | --non-interactive                     # interaction pin aliases
 274| --attach                                              # human attach if resolved interactive; NOT an auto pin (I-20)
 275| --max-turns N                                         # interactive only; env `SB_AGENT_MAX_TURNS` (CLI wins when present) (I-55)
 276| --max-wall-sec N                                      # wave-scoped wall (interactive); ignored on NI (I-51); host defaults in §5.2 (Claude/Codex 900, Cursor 1800, OpenCode/Pi 900)
 277| --idle-sec N                                          # interactive: quiet/idle before `stuck`; NI: feeds D7 tail-idle (I-51); reuses existing quiet/idle env (override)
 278| --allow-mode-fallback                                 # **pinned interactive only** → NI if TUI missing; one hop; audit `mode_fallback` {from,to,reason,flag} as `mode.json` `reason[]` token `mode_fallback:interactive→non-interactive:<cause>:<via>` (NI: this is the only sink; no `events.jsonl`) (I-56). **Not valid on D4** (would be a second NI) (I-25). On that hop, drop `--attach` / `--control-dir` / `--max-turns` / `--auto-policy` and record `fallback_drop:<flag>` in `reason[]` (I-61). Auto classified-interactive TUI-miss uses the same drop set without this flag (I-66).
 279| --auto-policy parent|brief_only|supervised            # interactive only; default supervised
 280| --no-escalate                                         # disable auto NI→interactive retry AND prior-wave force-interactive

