 382| ## 11. Risks
 383| 
 384| - **Classifier error (false NI)** mitigated by D4 one-shot escalate; **false interactive** costs a PTY — keep D3 rules tight (no implied test-fix loop) and tie-break NI.
 385| - **Cursor/Pi may lack a true TUI.** Auto tries NI with `tui-unavailable`; **pin** without `--allow-mode-fallback` stops at `mode-unavailable`; with fallback, audited NI hop (I-56/I-63). **D4** stops at `escalate-unavailable` + original NI FAIL, not `mode-unavailable`. Do not fake an expect wrapper.
 386| - **Deadlock** on interactive fifos: idle watchdog.
 387| - **PTY vs Cursor Task:** parent must hold the driver subprocess on `tui` hosts; Cursor interactive is session-id follow-up (new process allowed).
 388| - **Cost of escalate:** always one extra interactive run after a miss — disable in CI via `--no-escalate` if needed.
 389| - **Security:** snapshots **and** `events.jsonl` `assistant`/`tool_use` redacted; gitignored under `.planning/`.
 390| - **Overhead regressions:** tests assert NI process tree has no expect/tmux/fifo; allowed wrappers are preflight/quota/tail-idle only.
 391| - **Permission smash:** tests assert `--mode` never stores interaction values.
 392| 
 393| ## 12. Acceptance of this enhancement (later implementation)
 394| 
 395| - All five skills document auto + both modes, session-continuity rule, NI→interactive escalate, and lightweight NI.
 396| - Bare invoke without `--interaction-mode` records `mode_resolved` in `mode.json` from the classifier (not a hardcoded host default).
 397| - Explicit **concrete** `--interaction-mode interactive|non-interactive` (or pin alias / legacy pin) skips classify and skips escalate, and wins over D3; explicit `--interaction-mode auto` is requested-auto (classifier runs; escalate rules still apply).
 398| - Auto NI product miss performs exactly one interactive retry (unless `--no-escalate` or TUI unavailable).
 399| - NI path never opens a TUI/PTY/fifo/`events.jsonl` in tests; writes `mode.json` only.
 400| - Interactive Claude (or Codex) test: `question` → `ctl.sh send` → `result.md`.
 401| - Conflicting `--interaction-mode interactive --use-print` fails closed; `--mode non-interactive` fails closed (`mode-conflict`).
 402| - `--mode permissive --interaction-mode auto` is valid (orthogonal).
 403| - First-wave implement+test fixture classifies NI (D3 not fired).
 404| - Leftover conversation id after terminal `result.md` (no continue utterance) classifies fresh / NI — not D3 (I-18).
 405| - `--interaction-mode auto --attach` does not skip the classifier; classified NI fails `mode-conflict` (`attach-on-ni`) (I-20). Classified interactive then TUI miss hops to NI with `fallback_drop:attach` (and `fallback_drop:control-dir` when `--control-dir` was present), not `attach-on-ni` (I-66).
 406| - Inherited concrete `SB_AGENT_INTERACTION_MODE` without argv `--interaction-mode` fails `mode-conflict` (`leftover-env-pin`) (I-21).
 407| - Prior-wave after PASS classifies fresh; `--no-escalate` disables in-flight-escalate force-interactive only — it does **not** disable D3 (1) process-alive or D3 (2) continue/coach keep-alive on a reused task-id.
 408| - Cursor interactive fixture: follow-up is a new process with the same session id.
 409| - Auto + Pi/Cursor TUI missing → NI `tui-unavailable`, not fail-closed. If `--attach` / `--control-dir` (or `SB_AGENT_MODE_ATTACH`) were accepted because classified interactive, that hop drops them with `fallback_drop:<flag>` (same I-61 tokens as I-56); do not fail `attach-on-ni` / `control-dir-on-ni` and do not retain the flags or create `control/` (I-66).
 410| - Pinned interactive + TUI missing without `--allow-mode-fallback` → `mode-unavailable` (not silent NI) (D6, I-62).
 411| - Pinned interactive + TUI missing with `--allow-mode-fallback` → NI whose `mode.json` `reason[]` carries `mode_fallback:interactive→non-interactive:tui-unavailable:<via>`; `{interaction_mode:auto, allow_mode_fallback:true}` → `fallback-not-pinned` (I-56/I-57/I-59, I-62).
 412| - `events.jsonl` `assistant`/`tool_use` are redacted like snapshots.
 413| - AF-AGENT-DELEGATE seed round-trips `interaction_mode` including `auto`, plus `max_wall_sec` and `idle_sec` (same names as §6.2 / §8) (I-43).

